  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Locally-led nutrition interventions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sudan is currently experiencing a humanitarian crisis of disastrous proportions. After a year of conflict, tens of thousands of people have died. Around 6.7 million people have been internally displaced and over two million people have fled the country. Around 25 million people (over half of the population) are in need of humanitarian aid. In particular, the country suffers from a catastrophic hunger crisis. The national cereal availability gap is estimated at two million tons. As a result parts of the country are facing a risk of famine.The goal of this project is to identify and support locally-led nutrition activities that build upon existing projects to contribute to the local food and nutrition security situation in Sudan.</narrative>
  </description>
